  "name": "Aurawra",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Aurawra is an annual furry convention in Sydney, Australia, run by the staff of FurJAM and other organizers from New South Wales furry events under the NSW Anthro Group. Its name references Australia and the aurora australis, and its mascots are Aster the Crocodile, Billiam the Bilby and Quortney the Quoll. It was announced at FurJAM in September 2019 and planned for July 2020, but was delayed several times; an online event with a digital dealers' den and virtual fursuit walk was held in 2020, and a Twitch streaming event in 2021. The first in-person Aurawra took place July 22 to 24, 2022, at the PARKROYAL Parramatta, and attendance has grown from 324 to over 1,100 in 2025.",
